{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc | sed -n '1344,1362p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md | sed -n '80,105p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc | sed -n '45,105p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1344\t\n  1345\t(deftest shared-subgraphs-are-minted-once\n  1346\t  (testing \"a deep doubling chain mints once per source entity\"\n  1347\t    (let [depth 40\n  1348\t          ds (datoms-of (doubling-chain depth))\n  1349\t          entities (count (distinct (keep (fn [[e a]] (when (= :yin/type a) e)) ds)))\n  1350\t          counted (d/project-datoms-counted ds)]\n  1351\t      (is (= (inc (* 2 depth)) entities)\n  1352\t          \"one entity per level, one per level's `f`, and the leaf\")\n  1353\t      (is (= entities (:mints counted))\n  1354\t          \"one mint per [eid lexical-context] occurrence, never one per\n  1355\t           unfolded path — 2^40 paths here\")\n  1356\t      (is (= (+ depth 2) (count (:records counted)))\n  1357\t          \"the levels, the leaf, and one hash-consed free `f`\")\n  1358\t      ;; never compare :root here: it is a 2^40-leaf tree under structural\n  1359\t      ;; sharing, and = over two separately built copies walks every leaf\n  1360\t      (is (= (select-keys (d/project-datoms ds) [:fingerprint :records])\n  1361\t             (select-keys counted [:fingerprint :records]))\n  1362\t          \"the counted seam is output-neutral\")))\n    80\t| `:vm/current-continuation` | none | none |\n    81\t| `:vm/park` | none | none |\n    82\t| `:vm/resume` | `:yin/parked-id`, `:yin/val-node` | value |\n    83\t| `:stream/make` | `:yin/buffer` | none |\n    84\t| `:stream/put` | `:yin/target`, `:yin/val-node` | target, value |\n    85\t| `:stream/cursor`, `:stream/next`, `:stream/close` | source | source |\n    86\t\n    87\tThe table is exactly the emitter's vocabulary. `:yin/tail?` is derived\n    88\tcontrol-position data: it is ignored, excluded from rows and hashes, and is\n    89\tnot persisted by this projection.\n    90\t\n    91\tThe walk follows fixed child order. A vector is ordered data, never a set. A\n    92\tshared source entity is memoized by `[source-eid lexical-context]`, where\n    93\t`lexical-context` is the complete stack of frame parameter vectors. This memo\n    94\tis only an optimisation; it must never affect output identity. A finite AST\n    95\tgraph is required; cycles are rejected.\n    96\t\n    97\t## 3. Scope and de Bruijn resolution\n    98\t\n    99\tThe scope stack contains ordered parameter vectors. Frame depth `0` is the\n   100\tinnermost frame; position is the source parameter index, with the leftmost\n   101\tparameter at position `0`. Entering a lambda pushes one frame and leaving its\n   102\tbody pops it. The lambda's names are otherwise discarded; its binder becomes\n   103\tan arity.\n   104\t\n   105\tResolution searches frames from inner to outer. Within one frame it searches\n    45\t\n    46\t(def ^:private min-safe-id\n    47\t  \"Lowest integer exactly representable by every supported host (a JS\n    48\t   number's safe range). Code tempids stay at or above it so the ids of one\n    49\t   segment are distinct on CLJ, CLJS, and CLJD alike.\"\n    50\t  -9007199254740991)\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- reject-host-value!\n    54\t  [source attr v]\n    55\t  (when-not (vm/plain-data? v)\n    56\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Cannot lower a host value into \" attr)\n    57\t                    {:node source, :attr attr, :value v}))))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- flatten-program\n    61\t  \"The §5.3 flattening from `root`. Returns `[code labels]`: `code` is a\n    62\t   vector of `{:op :source :operands [[attr v] ..]}` in pc order, and `labels`\n    63\t   maps each label to the pc it marks.\"\n    64\t  [get-attr root]\n    65\t  (let [code (atom [])\n    66\t        labels (atom {})\n    67\t        bodies (atom [])\n    68\t        label-count (atom 0)\n    69\t        fresh! #(swap! label-count inc)\n    70\t        mark! (fn [l] (swap! labels assoc l (count @code)))\n    71\t        emit! (fn [source op & operands]\n    72\t                (let [operands (partition 2 operands)]\n    73\t                  (doseq [[a v] operands\n    74\t                          :when (not (contains? label-attrs a))]\n    75\t                    (reject-host-value! source a v))\n    76\t                  (swap! code conj\n    77\t                         {:op op, :source source, :operands operands})))]\n    78\t    (letfn\n    79\t      [(lower-node\n    80\t         [e]\n    81\t         (let [type (get-attr e :yin/type)]\n    82\t           (reject-unsupported! type e)\n    83\t           (case type\n    84\t             :literal (emit! e :const :yin.code/value (get-attr e :yin/value))\n    85\t             :variable (emit! e :var :yin.code/name (get-attr e :yin/name))\n    86\t             :lambda (let [l (fresh!)]\n    87\t                       (swap! bodies conj [l e (get-attr e :yin/body)])\n    88\t                       (emit! e :closure\n    89\t                              :yin.code/params (get-attr e :yin/params)\n    90\t                              :yin.code/body l))\n    91\t             :application (let [operands (get-attr e :yin/operands)]\n    92\t                            (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/operator))\n    93\t                            (emit! e :push)\n    94\t                            (doseq [o operands]\n    95\t                              (lower-node o)\n    96\t                              (emit! e :push))\n    97\t                            (emit! e :call\n    98\t                                   :yin.code/argc (count operands)\n    99\t                                   :yin.code/tail? (boolean\n   100\t                                                     (get-attr e :yin/tail?))))\n   101\t             :if (let [else (fresh!)\n   102\t                       end (fresh!)]\n   103\t                   (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/test))\n   104\t                   (emit! e :branch-false :yin.code/target else)\n   105\t                   (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/consequent))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
